# ============================================================
# Sea Birds Catalogue API — local / deploy environment notes
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# NO real secrets are committed to this repo. This file shows
# what an admin needs at deploy / seed time.
# ============================================================

# Wrangler authentication (set in your shell, never in the repo)
# Used for: wrangler dev, wrangler d1 migrations apply, wrangler pages deploy
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=<token with D1/R2/KV/Pages write scope>
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=<cloudflare account id>

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin password seeding (run locally, never committed)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Hash the first admin password on your own machine:
#      node scripts/hash-password.mjs 'choose-a-strong-password'
# 2. Copy the printed `pbkdf2$100000$...` string.
# 3. Either:
#    a) replace the PENDING_SEED__RUN_SCRIPTS_HASH_PASSWORD value in
#       migrations/0002_seed.sql BEFORE the first migration, or
#    b) apply the seed, then update the row directly:
#         wrangler d1 execute sea_birds_db --config ../wrangler.toml \
#           --command "UPDATE admin_users SET password_hash = 'pbkdf2$100000$...' WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';"
# 4. NEVER commit the resulting hash, and never put real admin
#    credentials in this repo.

# The seeded admin email is a placeholder; change it with:
#   UPDATE admin_users SET email = 'you@yourbusiness.in' WHERE id = 1;

# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is a Worker var (set in ../wrangler.toml, created by the
# parent orchestrator) — the public base URL of the IMAGES bucket, e.g.
# "https://images.sea-birds.example.com". Used to build file_url values for
# uploaded catalogue PDFs. Placeholder value is fine until DNS is set up.
